<title>UK: Limited rains in UK growing areas but more to come.</title>
<headline>Limited rains in UK growing areas but more to come.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unsettled weather over Britain's holiday weekend failed to bring much relief to farmers in parched eastern areas, weather analysts said on Monday.</p>
<p>The past 24 hours brought just two-three millimetres of rain to key producing areas of East Anglia -- in stark contrast with the eight millimetres that fell just outside the region on Sunday, according to the London Weather Centre.</p>
<p>But grain and beet producers can expect more rain in the next few days.</p>
<p>&quot;There will be more (rain) coming along this week,&quot; a spokeswoman at the centre said.</p>
